1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,805
At exactly twelve o'clock, his coffee floated out of the cup.

2
00:00:05,055 --> 00:00:07,131
Then the cup floated up after it.

3
00:00:07,281 --> 00:00:09,221
Then the chair. Then him.

4
00:00:09,671 --> 00:00:12,491
And nobody on the street looked surprised.

5
00:00:12,641 --> 00:00:15,529
They just checked their watches... and waited.

6
00:00:16,079 --> 00:00:19,678
Sixty seconds later, everything came back down.

7
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:24,548
Because in this town, every day at noon, gravity switches off.

8
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:26,512
For exactly one minute.

9
00:00:31,562 --> 00:00:33,603
Everybody knows the rules.

10
00:00:33,853 --> 00:00:38,655
At eleven fifty-nine, the bell in the old clock tower rings once.

11
00:00:39,005 --> 00:00:40,793
You buckle into a bench.

12
00:00:40,843 --> 00:00:42,742
You put a lid on your drink.

13
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:44,652
You hold on to your dog.

14
00:00:45,002 --> 00:00:47,329
And you wait for the bell to ring again.

15
00:00:49,579 --> 00:00:51,482
He got used to it fast.

16
00:00:53,279 --> 00:00:58,539
On day three, he forgot the lid. So he drank his coffee straight out of the air.

17
00:01:00,289 --> 00:01:03,727
On day eleven, his dog found out it could fly.

18
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:10,365
By day twenty-six, he could do a triple flip before the bell.

19
00:01:12,915 --> 00:01:17,007
And on day fifty-eight, he noticed something nobody else did.

20
00:01:17,257 --> 00:01:22,680
Every day at eleven fifty-eight, the same old woman climbed the clock tower.

21
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:27,715
And every day at twelve oh one, she came back down... a little slower.

22
00:01:29,865 --> 00:01:32,647
On day sixty-one, the bell didn't ring.

23
00:01:32,897 --> 00:01:35,846
Nobody buckled in. Nobody noticed.

24
00:01:35,996 --> 00:01:37,229
Except him.

25
00:01:37,779 --> 00:01:40,691
At noon, the whole town rose into the air.

26
00:01:40,941 --> 00:01:43,332
Ten seconds. Thirty. Sixty.

27
00:01:43,682 --> 00:01:45,797
And the bell... stayed silent.

28
00:01:46,247 --> 00:01:48,284
Gravity wasn't coming back.

29
00:01:48,534 --> 00:01:52,071
Everyone was drifting higher. Toward the clouds.

30
00:01:52,421 --> 00:01:59,548
So he grabbed a lamppost, pushed off as hard as he could, and swam through the sky to the clock tower.

31
00:02:01,198 --> 00:02:04,050
Inside, the old woman was fast asleep.

32
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,878
And behind her was the biggest key he had ever seen.

33
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:12,751
It was stuck in a giant spring. And the spring was almost empty.

34
00:02:13,301 --> 00:02:14,920
That's when he understood.

35
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:17,828
Gravity never switched off on its own.

36
00:02:17,978 --> 00:02:21,357
Someone had to wind it up. Every single day.

37
00:02:21,607 --> 00:02:24,499
And for sixty years, that someone was her.

38
00:02:25,049 --> 00:02:27,215
So he grabbed the key, and turned it.

39
00:02:27,365 --> 00:02:29,296
One turn. Two. Three.

40
00:02:29,646 --> 00:02:32,384
And the whole town came gently back down.

41
00:02:34,334 --> 00:02:37,284
When the old woman woke up, she just smiled.

42
00:02:37,534 --> 00:02:41,517
She handed him a tiny brass key on a string, and a note.

43
00:02:41,967 --> 00:02:44,145
It said: same time tomorrow.

44
00:02:45,245 --> 00:02:49,454
On his way out, he noticed four words carved under the keyhole.

45
00:02:50,304 --> 00:02:52,456
Never. Wind. It. Backwards.
